Ladybird accepts a numeric weight before the size in the font shorthand
in both document modes. Only the font-size longhand accepts a nonzero
unitless size in quirks mode.

The Gecko font shorthand uses FontSize::parse(). Blink parses the size
with css_parsing_utils::ConsumeFontSize() in ConsumeFont(). WebKit does
so in PropertyParserCustom::consumeFontShorthand().

Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 accepted numeric
weights of 100 and 450, zero sizes, and an optional line height. All
rejected a nonzero unitless shorthand size in both modes.
